    <string name="faq_section_plans">Relay and plans</string>
    <string name="faq_account_question">Do I need an account?</string>
    <string name="faq_account_answer">No. Each device makes its own identity and keeps its key in its own secure storage. There is no sign-up and no email.</string>
    <string name="faq_pair_question">How do I pair a Mac?</string>
    <string name="faq_pair_answer">Somebody has to be at the Mac. Choose it from the list when both are on the same network. The Mac shows six digits: enter them on the phone and continue only if they match. You pair once, and the devices reconnect on their own after that.</string>
    <string name="faq_mac_needs_question">What does the Mac need?</string>
    <string name="faq_mac_needs_answer">The Peering host app, running, with Screen Recording allowed so it can capture the screen, and Accessibility allowed so it can move the pointer and type.</string>
    <string name="faq_away_question">Can I connect away from home?</string>
    <string name="faq_away_answer">Yes. The phone first looks for a direct path between the two devices. If the networks will not allow one, the relay carries the session instead.</string>
    <string name="faq_awake_question">Does my Mac have to be awake?</string>
    <string name="faq_awake_answer">It has to be on to hold a session. A sleeping Mac cannot be woken from the phone.</string>
    <string name="faq_free_question">What is free?</string>
    <string name="faq_free_answer">Connecting over your own network, with no limit. The relay, which reaches a Mac on another network, is free for 30 minutes a day. Paid plans remove that limit.</string>
    <string name="faq_run_out_question">What happens when my relay time runs out?</string>
    <string name="faq_run_out_answer">The relay stops carrying new sessions until the next day. Connections on your own network keep working.</string>
    <string name="faq_subscribe_question">Why does the app ask me to subscribe?</string>
    <string name="faq_subscribe_answer">It asks after your first session, and again when your daily relay time is nearly gone. Dismissing it costs nothing, and nothing is charged unless you confirm it through the store.</string>
